# How to cite this software, read by GitHub ("Cite this repository"). Zenodo, which archives every
# GitHub release, uses .zenodo.json instead whenever it exists and ignores this file: the two are
# not combined, so .zenodo.json carries its own complete metadata (creators, licence, keywords).
# Keep both in step with each other and this version with pyproject.toml (tested).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Postcode-SIMD reference tables"
abstract: >-
  A CLI pipeline that attaches every edition of the Scottish Index of Multiple Deprivation (2004 to
  2020v2), its domains and the Urban Rural Classification to the NRS Scottish Postcode Directory and
  Scottish Statistics Postcode Lookup, from hash-pinned public sources, with a column-level
  provenance site.
authors:
  - family-names: Tinti
    given-names: Michele
    affiliation: "Health Informatics Centre (HIC), University of Dundee"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0051-017X"
version: "6.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23120390"   # the concept DOI: every release; each release also has its own
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtinti/postcode-simd"
url: "https://mtinti.github.io/postcode-simd/"
keywords:
  - SIMD
  - Scottish Index of Multiple Deprivation
  - postcode
  - deprivation
  - urban rural classification
  - data linkage
  - Scotland
